A||N||14||SloPonti||making the headlights stay up||||5
Z||000000||SloPonti||10-02-1999||06:26 PM||||in my dads nissian 300zx he has a button to push which will make the headlights stay up but he can turn off the headlights! this works great if you are just running into a store or something quick and it saves your headlight motors! does anyone know how to make one of these button thingys and how to wire it in? let me know<BR>thanks||||reg||5
Z||000001||Patrick||10-02-1999||08:42 PM||||<BR>This may come as a shock, but guess what, Fieros come with this feature!<P>I know, I know, it probably wasn't available every year, but my '87 has it and it's great.<P>||||reg||4
Z||000002||sluppy123||10-02-1999||08:49 PM||||What model is your 87'???  My 87' GT doesn't have a switch like that. The only way I can get them to stay up is to unplug the connector under the hood.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Patrick||10-02-1999||08:55 PM||||<BR>sluppy, I have just the base coupe.<P>I didn't realize that I had this feature either until I accidently didn't turn off the headlight switch "properly". When you go to turn off your headlights, move the switch as <B>little</B> as possible and see what happens. You may be surprised.<P>||||reg||4
Z||000004||theogre||10-02-1999||09:03 PM||||installing a toggle switch in one of the lines off the head light switch will do exactly this. I forget just wich line it is. pull out the switch, and hook a meter to each line. when you trun off the lights one of them goes hot. that's the line you interupt to keep the lights up.<P>Keeping the lights up in slushy weather is a real good idea. you get a bunch of ice formed down in there and the things get beat to heck......<P>As for the switch thing Patrick is doing.... Likely your switch is worn a bit, letting you shut it off w/o hitting the down contact. Lucky you. A good switch usually won't want to stay in that position..... I wouldn't use it like that often. It could decide to sudenly drop when you aren't expecting it to.||||reg||1
Z||000005||TOM||10-02-1999||09:23 PM||||I added a switch for this purpose. Its easy just tap into the white wire from the switch. I mounted the switch under the dash to keep it neat. I have since added the headlight mod so its all a moot point.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Patrick||10-02-1999||09:27 PM||||<BR>You mean it's NOT supposed to do this?<P>Well, I guess this makes up for the hell I've gone through with my clutch hydraulics. No, wait a sec, <B>nothing</B> could make up for that!<P>||||reg||10
Z||000007||David||10-02-1999||10:00 PM||||I installed the switch this past weekend to keep my lights up.  It is indeed the white wire coming off of the headlight switch.  I installed my switch above the rear window defroster switch to the right of the dash.  It took about 20-30 minutes to complete the job.||||reg||1
Z||000008||theogre||10-03-1999||06:33 PM||||I'm going to add that switch before winter..... we get allot of slushy crap around here.<P>Another thing to remember...... make sure you break any ice on the doors, and lift the hood to check the lights in icy weather. Otherwise they might get jammed when opening.||||reg||1
Z||000009||WGraffiKs||10-04-1999||03:11 PM||||If you simply shut off the gray switch without toggling the whole black part too, the headlights go off but the doors remain up.  I believe the parking lights will stay on, though, unless the black switch is turned off.  I use my thumb on the rounded part of the gray switch to turn it off by itself.(pull it outward)  Will the "white-wire" mod turn off the parking lights too (as well as the "PONTIAC" tail advertisement on fastbacks)?||||reg||1
Z||000010||theogre||10-04-1999||04:21 PM||||The regular switch function doesn't change. When the regular switch is all the way off, the 'white-wire' modification interupts the line to the down side of the head light motor circuit. This lets you kill power to all the lamps, but the lights can't close.<P>The only thing to remember is that if someone later hits the added switch the lights will drop down. So don't be working on the lights if someone is around to hit the new switch.<P>With or without the modification you should always unplug the light motors when working on the headlights to change bulbs and such.||||reg||1
Z||000011||Patrick||10-05-1999||02:28 AM||||<BR>When I commented earlier on my Fiero's ability to turn off it's headlights without having to flip them down, I erroneously reported how I did it. It's one of those things that you can't remember properly because it has become such an automatic thing to do.<P>When I turn off my headlights, I flip the toggle switch down with a definite "click". However, unless I also continue to press the bottom part of the toggle switch once it's in the <B>Off</B> position, the headlights will NOT go down. If, while pressing the switch, I release this pressure while the headlights are going down, they will instantly stop right where they are. If I continue to press, they will naturally go all the way down.<P>I suspect Ogre will say that I was hallucinating or something, but I am almost positive I read somewhere that this is "normal", but that this feature just wasn't always available. <P>Isn't there anyone else out there whose Fiero is able to do this? <P>I feel so ..... different .....  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">||||reg||4
Z||000012||Phil||10-05-1999||08:40 AM||||My 88 Formula does the same thing but I do think it is a malfuntioning switch. When the lights are off and the doors stay up the big blue dingy thingy(from another post)does its thing(y). My 85 and 88 GTs wont do it.||||reg||1
Z||000013||Patrick||10-05-1999||03:27 PM||||<BR>If this ability is due to a malfunctioning switch, I wish more components would malfunction in this way on my Fiero. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> ||||reg||14
Z||000014||theogre||10-05-1999||03:55 PM||||If that's all that's wrong with it cool. I'd still consider it a defective switch. As long as it can't drop by itself w/o warning or someone pushing on the switch...... it doesn't pose much danger, and if it works the way you want it to so much the better.||||reg||1
